-- title:
--   Pic⁰-representing scheme is locally of finite type
-- statement:
--   Let $R$ be a Noetherian commutative ring, let $c \colon C \to \operatorname{Spec} R$ be a morphism of schemes that is proper, smooth of relative dimension $1$ and geometrically integral, and let $\varepsilon$ be a section of $c$, i.e. a morphism $\operatorname{Spec} R \to C$ whose composite with $c$ is the identity. Assume that finite-map data for $(c,\varepsilon)$ exist with arbitrarily large degree: for every $m_0 \in \mathbb{N}$ there is a datum $\mathfrak{F}$ consisting of two affine opens $U,V \subseteq C$ with $U \sqcup V = \top$, where $U$ is exactly the complement of the image of $\varepsilon$, sections $f \in \Gamma(C,U)$ and $g \in \Gamma(C,V)$ with $U \sqcap V$ equal both to the basic open set of $f$ and to that of $g$ and with the restrictions of $f$ and $g$ to $U \sqcap V$ multiplying to $1$, such that $\Gamma(C,U)$ is finite over $R[T]$ via $T \mapsto f$ and $\Gamma(C,V)$ is finite over $R[T]$ via $T \mapsto g$, and such that for every local $R$-algebra $S$ and every $s \in S$ the quotient $S \otimes_R \Gamma(C,U)$ by the ideal generated by $1 \otimes f - s \otimes 1$ is a finite free $S$-module of rank $\mathfrak{F}.m$, with $m_0 \le \mathfrak{F}.m$. Let $D$ consist of a scheme $D.P$ with structure morphism $D.\mathrm{toBase} \colon D.P \to \operatorname{Spec} R$ and a section $D.\mathrm{zeroSection}$ of it, and suppose $D$ represents the sub-Picard condition `algEquivZeroCut`: there is a rigidified line bundle on $C \times_{\operatorname{Spec} R} D.P$ (invertible, with trivialised pullback along the rigidifying section) whose restriction to every fibre over an algebraically closed point is algebraically equivalent to zero, which is universal in the sense that for every $t \colon T \to \operatorname{Spec} R$ and every rigidified line bundle $M$ on $C \times_{\operatorname{Spec} R} T$ with the same fibrewise condition there is a unique morphism $T \to D.P$ over $\operatorname{Spec} R$ pulling the Poincaré bundle back to a bundle isomorphic to $M.L$, and whose pullback along $D.\mathrm{zeroSection}$ is isomorphic to the unit bundle. Then $D.\mathrm{toBase}$ is locally of finite type.
--
--   This is the finiteness half of the construction of the Jacobian of a pointed smooth proper geometrically integral curve: once a scheme $D$ representing the relative $\mathrm{Pic}^0$ functor (line bundles algebraically equivalent to zero on all geometric fibres, rigidified along $\varepsilon$) has been produced, its structure morphism to $\operatorname{Spec} R$ is locally of finite type. It is used in the existence statement for such a representing scheme over reduced bases, [`AlgebraicGeometry.RelPicard.exists_representsRelSubPic_algEquivZeroCut_of_finiteMapData_of_isReduced`](thm.html#AlgebraicGeometry.RelPicard.exists_representsRelSubPic_algEquivZeroCut_of_finiteMapData_of_isReduced).
